      <h1 class="jr-h1">Oral Sunscreen: Does a Pill Really Protect You From the Sun?</h1>
      <p class="jr-standfirst">Sunscreen pills are sold on the promise that protection can be swallowed, and the ingredient behind most of them is a fern extract with real trials behind it. Here is what those trials actually measured, the arithmetic nobody publishes next to the claim, and why a regulator wrote to four companies about it.</p>

